{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"src/js.rs","issuer":"seat:personal-fold-core-goal","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T17:41:33.897572Z","id":"52a3439ddce3c4972828782f80acc9f374223b3cf9a221e0635afd1b023bbf3b","body":{"detail":"walk ranks findings by fold id with localeCompare (ICU root collation). The port reproduces ICU's ASCII order (punctuation, digits, letters, case as a tie-break) and orders anything past ASCII by code point after it, where ICU interleaves (é sorts between e and f). Fold ids are slugs today, so goldens cannot see it; an artifact id or page key with non-ASCII would rank differently.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:42b4f3d","suggested_fix":"if ids ever carry non-ASCII, use icu_collator (root, alternate non-ignorable) and add a golden with such ids","summary":"locale_compare matches bun's localeCompare for ASCII only","tags":["parity","session:claude-code:0345f693-a48d-478f-aa49-1df22880dff2"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"src/walk.rs","issuer":"seat:personal-fold-core-goal","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T17:41:33.902256Z","id":"366530d7b56f9fc7dc9bed41f895d40b9c3fcea707c7382292e4a22b2147344f","body":{"detail":"For round 3 (home switches the gate's walk onto the core): the caller passes JSON.parse(budgets.json).budgets as opts.budgets and its own zone as opts.localTimeZone, as fold.ts already passes localTimeZone to fold_json. A budgets file without view.words is an error ({error: 'budgets: no view.words'}), where walk.ts would throw on undefined.","kind":"comment","ref":"git:42b4f3d","summary":"walk takes budgets.json's budgets as input; home's walk.ts reads the file itself","tags":["round-3","session:claude-code:0345f693-a48d-478f-aa49-1df22880dff2"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"src/tz.rs","issuer":"seat:personal-fold-core-goal","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:07:04.206480Z","id":"cf696dc6719924f73b67e10a7d425f71965f6caca543a4a700d03b9cbffbed9f","body":{"detail":"Since 505eea4 the module needs the import js/fold-core.ts core() provides (Intl-backed). home's programs/fold-viewer/core.ts instantiates with {} and would fail to link on its next pin bump: round 3 must switch it to core() or supply the import. Allie's WKWebView has Intl, so the same loader works there.","kind":"comment","ref":"git:505eea4","summary":"the wasm module imports fold_core.tz_offset; a host must answer it","tags":["round-3","session:claude-code:0345f693-a48d-478f-aa49-1df22880dff2"]}}
